cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tycheon in research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Tycheon: calibrated forecasting and risk analytics"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Tycheon is an open-source library that adds calibrated uncertainty (conformal prediction
  intervals) and forecast-to-risk translation (VaR, Expected Shortfall, drawdown probability)
  on top of forecasting models such as Kronos, with leakage-proof walk-forward evaluation and a
  random-walk baseline reported with every result. For research and risk analytics. Not
  investment advice.
authors:
  - family-names: Prasad
    given-names: Anil
    affiliation: Ambharii Labs
repository-code: "https://github.com/anilatambharii/tycheon"
url: "https://github.com/anilatambharii/tycheon"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
keywords:
  - forecasting
  - time series
  - conformal prediction
  - calibration
  - value at risk
  - expected shortfall
  - backtesting
